amd64 (x86-64) port skeleton.

TODO:
- mk/arch/amd64/boot/linker.ld  — 64-bit ELF linker script (OUTPUT_FORMAT elf64-x86-64)
- mk/arch/amd64/boot/boot.s     — 64-bit multiboot2 entry (long mode setup: EFER.LME, paging, GDT)
- mk/arch/amd64/intr/           — 64-bit IDT, GDT, ISR, APIC
- mk/arch/amd64/thread/         — 64-bit context switch (swapgs-based)
- mk/arch/amd64/syscall/        — SYSCALL/SYSRET or SYSENTER/SYSEXIT handler
- mk/arch/amd64/include/        — arch-specific headers (segments.h, paging.h, regs.h)

Key differences from i386:
- Paging: PML4 → PDP → PD → PT (48-bit virtual, 52-bit physical)
- Interrupts: IDT with IST, APIC mandatory (no PIC)
- Syscalls: MSR-based (LSTAR, STAR, SF_MASK) instead of int 0x80
- Higher half: 0xFFFFFFFF80000000 (canonical) vs 0xC0000000
- ABI: System V x86-64 (register args: rdi, rsi, rdx, rcx, r8, r9)
